INT. PARKING GARAGE - LEVEL P4 - NIGHT

Concrete and sodium light. One car left, a black sedan with its trunk open. FRANCISCO MEDRANO (40s, courier jacket) and NINA VOLKOVA (30s, trench coat) stand on either side of it. Between them, a leather satchel on the floor.

                    FRANCISCO
          You said alone.

                    NINA
          I am alone.

A footstep echoes. Both turn. ROLAND BECK (50s, hands in pockets) steps out from behind a pillar.

                    ROLAND
          Not quite.

                    FRANCISCO
          You're early.

                    NINA
          You're late. Hand it over.

                    ROLAND
          Both of you, calm down.

                    FRANCISCO
          He's got a gun.

                    NINA
          I know he's got a gun.

She lunges for the satchel. He lunges for her wrist. They collide and go down, the satchel skidding across the concrete. Roland steps forward and plants a boot on it.

                    ROLAND
          That's enough. Both of you, up.

They rise slowly, breathing hard. Roland picks up the satchel and weighs it in his hand. Then he tosses it back at Francisco, and walks away.

                    NINA
          (staring after him)
          What was that?

Francisco unzips the satchel. Inside, it is empty.
